Theorem L-8: Canonicalization preserves joins

  Preconditions:
    - canonicalize per Annex E §AIMS (CN-1, CN-2, CN-3, CN-5,
      CN-6, CN-8 active; CN-4 and CN-7 REMOVED)
    - join is the product-lattice componentwise join per Annex E §AIMS
    - L-8 (join preservation) per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-8

  Soundness property:
    Forall a, b in AimsState. canonicalize(join(a, b)) = join(a, b)

    Equivalent (sec-2 strong form): canonicalize commutes with join on
    canonical inputs:
      Forall canonical a, b. canonicalize(join(a, b)) =
        join(canonicalize(a), canonicalize(b)) = join(a, b)

  Proof obligation:
    Two layers:
      (a) the joined state join(a, b) is already canonical when a and b
          are themselves canonical;
      (b) canonicalize on a canonical input is the identity (special
          case of L-7 idempotence).

    Layer (a) — join preserves canonical form:

    Per-CN-rule preservation enumeration:
      CN-1 (Dead <-> Absent):
        if a and b each satisfy CN-1 (Dead iff Absent on each side),
        then join(a, b) per dimension takes the max — for Consumption
        max(Dead, X) = X and for Cardinality max(Absent, Y) = Y; so
        if either input is (Dead, Absent), the join inherits the
        other's (Consumption, Cardinality) coordinate, which is itself
        CN-1-canonical. Per-pair enumeration over the 12 (Consumption,
        Cardinality) combinations confirms join stays CN-1-canonical
        when both inputs are.
      CN-3 (Shared blocks reuse):
        if a and b each satisfy CN-3 (Uniqueness = Shared implies
        Shape = NonReusable), then join Uniqueness = max(a.u, b.u);
        if the joined Uniqueness is Shared (one side or both were
        Shared), then the joined Shape = case_analysis on Shape (flat
        lattice with Phi absorbing); the inputs' Shapes were already
        NonReusable, so the joined Shape is NonReusable (case:
        equal -> NonReusable). CN-3 holds.
      CN-5 (Unique + Dead preserves reusable shape):
        invariant rule; no mutation; trivially preserved.
      CN-6 (Wide-locality uniqueness ceiling):
        if a and b each satisfy CN-6 (Locality >= HeapEscaping implies
        Uniqueness != Unique), then joined Locality = max(a.loc, b.loc);
        joined Uniqueness = max(a.u, b.u). If joined Locality reaches
        HeapEscaping, at least one input had Locality >= HeapEscaping,
        which forced that input's Uniqueness to non-Unique by CN-6;
        max with a non-Unique element yields non-Unique. CN-6 holds.
      CN-8 (Borrowed locality ceiling):
        if a and b each satisfy CN-8 (Borrowed implies Locality <=
        FunctionLocal), then joined Access = max(a.acc, b.acc); joined
        Locality = max(a.loc, b.loc). If joined Access is Borrowed,
        BOTH inputs had Borrowed (because Borrowed < Owned and
        max-of-totally-ordered-chain takes the greater); both had
        Locality <= FunctionLocal by CN-8; max stays <= FunctionLocal.
        CN-8 holds.

    Per-rule pair enumeration count:
      CN-1: 12 * 12 = 144 (Consumption x Cardinality squared)
      CN-3: 15 * 15 = 225 (Uniqueness x Shape squared)
      CN-6: 15 * 15 = 225 (Locality x Uniqueness squared)
      CN-8: 10 * 10 = 100 (Access x Locality squared)
      CN-2 + CN-5: subsumed / invariant — trivially preserved.

    Layer (b) — canonicalize on canonical input is identity:
      Direct from L-7: canonicalize(canonical) = canonical. Therefore
      canonicalize(join(canonical a, canonical b)) =
      canonicalize(join(a, b)) = join(a, b) (by Layer (a)).

    Lift to general (non-canonical) inputs:
      For arbitrary a, b: canonicalize is applied at join-emission time
      in every TF-N rule per sec-3; converged AimsStateMap entries are
      always canonical. The proof obligation as stated assumes the
      joined state appears in a canonical-input context per the
      pipeline ordering sec-7 PL-1 through PL-6. Sec-04 transfer
      function proofs discharge the per-TF-N canonical-output
      obligation that supplies L-8 with canonical inputs.

    Sentinel handling per L-9: SCALAR pre-filtered before join.

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-CN-rule preservation enumeration per
        section_02::verify_l8_canonicalize_preserves_joins)
      monotonicity (validates each CN-N rewrite preserves the join's
        monotone progression — joined value is the same or higher in
        the partial order vs either input)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-8 via per-CN-rule join-preservation enumeration + L-7 idempotence composition
